X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/third-thursday-11-5/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260521
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260522
DTSTAMP:20260515T235103
CREATED:20260414T144046Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260513T194810Z
UID:10005977-1779321600-1779407999@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Third Thursday: Small Business Appreciation Night featuring Jackson Grimm and Clint Roberts of Holler Choir
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Small Business Month at May’s Third Thursday until 9pm with a special Small Business Appreciation Night\, presented by Bank of America\, at the Asheville Art Museum. In conjunction with the exhibition In a New Light: American Impressionism 1870–1940\, Works from the Bank of America Collection\, enjoy an afternoon and evening of community connection featuring live music\, hands‑on creativity\, and more. \nAs the evening unfolds\, Asheville-based\, nationally recognized musicians Jackson Grimm and Clint Roberts will perform in the Museum’s Windgate Foundation Atrium from 6–8 pm. Grimm and Roberts—also members of the popular band Holler Choir—blend old-time and swing band traditions with indie rock\, creating a sound that’s both unique and deeply satisfying. \nSettle in and enjoy the music\, grab a drink from the Perspective Café pop‑up bar\, then stroll the galleries and experience your favorite artworks after hours. Don’t forget to stop by the Studio to silkscreen your own poster to take home—a creative keepsake from a night celebrating art\, music\, small businesses\, and our vibrant local community. \nABOUT THE MUSICIANS\n\nJackson Grimm is an accomplished and respected band leader\, multi-instrumentalist and teacher in the Western North Carolina music community. His songs marry folk pop melodies with the lonesome sound of traditional Appalachian music. In a region with a strong music culture\, it is no surprise that Grimm’s songwriting is representative of his musical birthplace: Asheville. \nGrimm won the 2025 LEAF Songwriting competition and has been a 2 year finalist for the Songwriter Serenade. He has shared the stage with and opened up for acts such as Molly Tuttle\, Sierra Ferrell\, Shadowgrass\, the Wilder Flower\, Arlo Guthrie\, Tim Grimm\, Ben Bedford\, Ordinary Elephant\, Nathan Evans Fox\, and more.” \nClint Roberts was raised in the Appalachian mountains of Western North Carolina and crafts songs that bridge the gap between the region’s deep-rooted folk traditions and the contemporary Americana heard on national airwaves. After dedicating a decade to his solo singer-songwriter career beginning in his early twenties\, Clint founded the collective-driven string band Holler Choir in Asheville in 2021. \nSince then\, Holler Choir has toured extensively across the United States and expanded its creative reach by becoming the backing band for a second project\, the Susto String Band\, formed in collaboration with the band Susto. In 2024\, songwriter and multi-instrumentalist Jackson Grimm joined both Holler Choir and the Susto String Band and now co-leads the project alongside Clint.
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/third-thursday-11-5/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Performance,Third Thursday
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/Grimm-and-Roberts.jpeg
GEO:35.5946714;-82.5512827
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Asheville Art Museum 2 South Pack Square Asheville NC 28801 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=2 South Pack Square:geo:-82.5512827,35.5946714
END:VEVENT
