X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/intro-to-mycology-mushrooms-101/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260528T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260528T150000
DTSTAMP:20260515T235115
CREATED:20260411T170529Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260411T170529Z
UID:10017185-1779973200-1779980400@www.ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Intro to Mycology: Mushrooms 101
DESCRIPTION:Intro to Mycology: Mushrooms 101\nwith Erin Canter \nThursday\, May 28  |  1 – 3pm \nBRN – Core  |  BREG – Elective \nREGISTER HERE \nThis basic beginners course to Mycology will focus on mushroom anatomy\, ecology\, and introduction to component parts useful in identification. This course will NOT focus on specific mushroom identification or foraging\, but rather serve to introduce participants to the diversity of mushroom types and characteristics\, including use of field guides. \nThis program will take place outside and will follow easy trails and paved walkways. Dress for the weather and prepare to be outside for the entire program time. \nErin Canter is a Southern Appalachian Naturalist who specializes in southeastern ecology. She worked as the Manager of Science Literacy and Research at a nonprofit education center in the Great Smoky Mountains\, working with all ages to explore their bioregion through science and hands on exploration\, before moving to this side of the mountains in early 2024. She now works at American Conservation Experience here in WNC\, helping young people begin their conservation careers through applied conservation projects in the region. \n\nMembers: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions.\nSee a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs.\nWe are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide.\nFollow us on Facebook & Instagram!\nJoin our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord!\nInterested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here.\n\nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/intro-to-mycology-mushrooms-101/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Adult-Ed-Course-Jpgs-22.jpg
END:VEVENT
