X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/spring-plant-sale-and-market-2/2026-05-29/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260529T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260529T150000
DTSTAMP:20260515T235115
CREATED:20260212T170948Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260428T203107Z
UID:10016919-1780048800-1780066800@www.ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Spring Plant Sale and Market
DESCRIPTION:Spring Plant Sale and Market\nFriday\, May 29 10:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m.\nSaturday\, May 30 10:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m.\nCalling all garden lovers! Join us on Friday and Saturday\, May 29-30 for our annual Spring Plant Sale and Market. The Market features unique plants grown in The North Carolina Arboretum’s Production Greenhouse and includes over 30 local growers and businesses. Shop an outstanding collection of annuals\, perennials and crafts to the sounds of live music. On Saturday\, May 30th\, children can participate in crafts at the Kids Corner. Rain or shine. The Arboretum’s standard parking fee applies for all non-members. Interested in joining as a member? Join today! \nThis year’s Spring Plant Sale & Market is packed with more than just plants — come for the knowledge\, live music\, and hands-on fun too! \n\n\nFree Soil Class — Drop into our Adult Education Class\, Soil Amendments & Natural Fertilizers\, both days from 11:30 a.m.–12:30 p.m. in the Education Center Classroom. No registration needed! \n\n\nLive Music & Shopping — Browse Arboretum-grown plants and 30+ local vendors to the sounds of live music\, 10:00 a.m.–3:00 p.m. both days. \n\n\nAsk A Gardener (Saturday\, May 30 only) — The NC State Extension Master Gardener Volunteers of Buncombe County will be on hand to answer your toughest plant care questions at their dedicated booth. \n\n\nFamily Activities (Saturday\, May 30\, 11:00 a.m.–2:00 p.m.) — Bring the kids! Enjoy the Kid’s Corner Crafts Tent\, Eco-Explorer activities at Willow Pond\, and plant crafts in the Education Center Auditorium. \n\n\nVendors\nAppalachian DiviniTEA\nAsheville Blue Ridge Rose Society\nB.B. Barns\nBear Necessities Farm\nBee. honey+hive   *Saturday only\nBellyfull Plants Nursery\nBest Friends Creations\nBlazing Star Flowers\nBlue Ridge Exotics\nBotanical Tortoise Co\nBridge & Tunnel Coffee Co\nConjure Craft Chocolate / Sweet Cub Soft Serve\nConnections Gallery Gift Shop\nFlower Moon Nursery\nHigh Country Nursery\nHomegrown Tropicals\nImladris Farm\nKindland Farm\nKW Edible Landscaping Nursery\nMaking Stuff\nNC State Extension Master Gardener Volunteers of Buncombe Co\nOpen Hearts Art Center\nResin8light\nSandy Mush Herb Nursery\nSaturnia Farm\nShiny Hand Soap Co\nSkipping Pibble Designs\nSky Gardens\nSloth and Crow Wood Craft\nSoil & Sun Studio\nSolstice Handmade\nSustainabillies\nTanager Plants\nThe Farm Connection\nThe Turquoise Tortuga\nWehrloom Honey\nWell Seasoned Table\nWoodWitchCrafts   *Saturday only\nThis event is part of Spring Into the Arb! Celebrate the return of spring with a series of events and happenings throughout March\, April\, May and June! Spring is a time of renewal and emergence\, and The North Carolina Arboretum is excited to welcome this season with plant shows\, nature programs\, education\, music\, art and more!
URL:https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/spring-plant-sale-and-market-2/2026-05-29/
LOCATION:Arboretum Tent | Parking Bay #3
CATEGORIES:Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Instagram-Post-93.jpg
END:VEVENT
